From 09bf1ca646a7182c3e4c5af93e9673c2bdd734db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 22:22:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] U10 review: refuse pins on set weeks, reject impossible
 dates, keep prettier off the map

- scripts/lib/family-year.mjs: a hand override on a week a daily seasonal set
  serves now stops the build with the reason. Before, the build accepted it
  and wrote a week carrying both a set and a devotion, which the type's own
  doc rules out and the map test then failed on with a bare "expected null".
- client/src/lib/familyYear.ts: onFamilyMap and the readers return null for a
  date that is not a real day ("2027-02-30"), as the doc comment promised;
  Date used to roll it into March and answer for the wrong week.
- .prettierignore: client/src/lib/*.generated.ts. The family map is not in
  Prettier's style, so a format-on-save or `pnpm format` would rewrite it
  and the new `build-family-year.mjs --check` CI step would then fail.
- Tests for the first two.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JuCQ8kZ25i9zRwNgk6bh4e
